      "problem": "Given the matrix\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14142972/assets/ed969afdc66f5a31b67a815c59fd0b7d5e6f3ba954bfe680e39609144cd6f256.svg) find the row operations that transform $A$ into the $3 \\times 3$ identity matrix.",
      "worked_solution": "We consider the augmented matrix $[A\\,|\\,I]$ where $I$ is the $3\\times 3$ identity. Applying the indicated row operations we have\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14142972/assets/21cee3d2eb8d524f2c5b3492ed4c55516c0b4021823307d6e52e7c2daa2daf1a.svg)\n\nTherefore, the required row operations are $R_3 := (-1) R_3$ and $R_1 := R_1+(-4)R_3,$ and inverse matrix is \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14142972/assets/7b54dff7b40bba73ef16461be404ed6a0cf35df98520ebe3c44b8eda0eaf5304.svg)",
